---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait3.jpg';
import { ExternalLink } from '../components/ExternalLink';
import { Projects } from '../components/Projects';
import { Section } from '../components/Section';
import { Work } from '../components/Work';
import { profile } from '../content/profile';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const { email } = profile;
const { github, linkedin, xing } = profile.links;
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div class="column pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <header class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <Picture
        src={portrait}
        alt={`Portrait of ${profile.name}`}
        width={64}
        height={64}
        fit="cover"
        position="top"
        densities={[1, 2, 3]}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        loading="eager"
        class="size-16 rounded-full bg-line object-cover"
      />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold">{profile.name}</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">
          {profile.role} in {profile.location}
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5">
      <p>
        I’ve been building software for about twenty years, most of it for the web and most of the
        last decade in TypeScript. I like owning a feature from the data model to the UI, so my days
        are split between React frontends, Node.js services, APIs and SQL.
      </p>
      <p>
        The part I keep coming back to is the frontend: applications with real complexity, the
        design systems behind them, and architectures that let several teams ship into one product.
        Most recently I spent three years on the frontend platform team of Lexware Office,
        maintaining the design system and building a micro-frontend architecture.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that I studied computer science at ETH Zürich and wrote Java enterprise software in
        Switzerland: point-of-sale systems for Swiss Federal Railways and PostFinance, then payment
        processing at SIX Group. I moved to Berlin in 2013. These days agentic AI tools are a normal
        part of how I work.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Projects />
    <Work />

    <Section id="contact" title="Contact">
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`} class="link">
          {email}
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        I’m also on <ExternalLink href={github.href}>{github.label}</ExternalLink>,{' '}
        <ExternalLink href={linkedin.href}>{linkedin.label}</ExternalLink> and{' '}
        <ExternalLink href={xing.href}>{xing.label}</ExternalLink>.
      </p>
    </Section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
